<title>ITALY: Olivetti denies any delays in PC sale.</title>
<headline>Olivetti denies any delays in PC sale.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's Olivetti on Wednesday denied that there was a delay in the sale of its personal computer company after a report in Milan daily Corriere della Sera said that a delay was possible.  </p>
<p>An Olivetti statement said that the sale of its PC company was forecast to take place by the end of this month, and it added that there were no obstacles to the sale.</p>
<p>Last month, Olivetti agreed to sell its loss-making PC company to Piedmont International, controlled by U.S. lawyer Edward Gottesman's Centenary Group.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
